& [SurfaceBoundaryMap: FSC4SurfaceBoundaryAndInvariantMapV1] is the imported surface boundary map for FSC4 surface projection
  + [slice_id] is FSC4-S01
  + [source_chunk] is FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [target_chunk] is FSC4 surface projection
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is docs/planning/FSC3_Runtime_Graph_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_boundary_input_sha256] is 6E03B128800FD6E8D9C2742141A9E884B1B6D7649D6D8F4B4AE78FEDB00AF58B
  + [import_policy] is read_only_import
  + [projection_policy] is surfaces may render and route projected records but cannot become source authority
  + [implementation_policy] is no UI, adapter, Langflow, transport, or operations implementation is authorized by this map alone

  = must: treat FSC1, FSC2, and FSC3 packs as accepted boundary inputs, not editable surface drafts
  = must: make every decision-making surface carry authority, freshness, lineage, and visible blocked/stale/fault/interrupt status
  = must: route authority-sensitive actions through accepted operator contracts, SOP-first interrupt, human override, or completion review gates
  - never: let surface state, adapter logs, chat messages, terminal output, or Langflow diagrams silently mutate source authority

& [ImportedSurfaceContractInventory] is the accepted contract inventory imported into FSC4
  + [imported_pack] is FSC1FoundationContractPackV1
  + [imported_pack] is FSC2PlanningCoordinationPackV1
  + [imported_pack] is FSC3RuntimeGraphProofPackV1
  + [imported_contract] is KernelRecord common field contract
  + [imported_contract] is work_packet_generation v1
  + [imported_contract] is coordination_claim_register v1
  + [imported_contract] is coordination_conflict_signal v1
  + [imported_contract] is completion_review_delta_gate v1
  + [imported_contract] is WholeFieldPlannerGraphContractV1
  + [imported_contract] is SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1
  + [imported_contract] is OperatorTraceRuntimeProofContractV1
  + [imported_contract] is HiddenWritePreventionProof
  + [imported_fixture_plan] is FSC3RuntimeGraphFixturePlanV1

  = must: preserve record_id, record_kind, natural_key, subject_ref, authority_state, source_ref_set, lineage_edge_set, freshness_rule, and status on projected records
  = must: preserve support_delta, requirement_delta, coordination claim, operator_trace, fault_record, stale_projection, interrupt_context, and completion review obligations

& [ProjectionOwnedInvariantSet] is the invariant set owned by FSC4
  + [invariant] is surface records are projections, not source authority
  + [invariant] is surface-local state is display and interaction state only
  + [invariant] is authority_notice is required anywhere a human or agent may make a decision from the projection
  + [invariant] is freshness_rule and stale state are visible before action is offered
  + [invariant] is blocked, faulted, interrupted, and pending-review states are visible and cannot be rendered as completed work
  + [invariant] is source_ref_set and lineage_edge_set remain inspectable from every decision-making projection
  + [invariant] is manager projection may summarize readiness but cannot assign or dispatch by itself
  + [invariant] is worker projection may display packet obligations but cannot claim completion by itself
  + [invariant] is narrative projection may summarize lineage but cannot rewrite source narrative authority
  + [invariant] is debug projection may inspect traces and faults but cannot repair authority without an accepted route
  + [invariant] is adapters are carriers and action classifiers, not authority stores
  + [invariant] is optional Langflow diagrams are explanatory projections, not executable authority by themselves
  + [invariant] is multi-surface divergence produces stale or conflict visibility before follow-on action

  = must: preserve these invariants through FSC4-S02 through FSC4-S07
  = must: mark downstream FSC4 slices stale when any invariant changes

& [SurfaceNonAuthorityBoundary] is the authority boundary for projected surface state
  + [not_authority] is browser component state
  + [not_authority] is dashboard cache
  + [not_authority] is chat transcript projection
  + [not_authority] is Codex thread display
  + [not_authority] is terminal output projection
  + [not_authority] is IRC channel log
  + [not_authority] is Matrix room event
  + [not_authority] is web adapter request state
  + [not_authority] is Langflow visual graph node
  + [not_authority] is local adapter queue
  + [authority_route] is signed source specification
  + [authority_route] is accepted canonical specification
  + [authority_route] is accepted proof_result
  + [authority_route] is accepted completion_review
  + [authority_route] is accepted human override record with authority notice
  + [authority_route] is SOP-first interrupt resolution with source_ref_set

  = must: reject any projection contract that promotes transport or UI state to authority without an accepted route
  = must: require authority_notice whenever projected state is lower authority than the action it may invite

& [AdapterMutationBoundary] is the mutation boundary for inbound actions from projected surfaces
  + [inbound_action_kind] is observation
  + [inbound_action_kind] is comment
  + [inbound_action_kind] is proposal
  + [inbound_action_kind] is work_request
  + [inbound_action_kind] is claim_request
  + [inbound_action_kind] is human_override_request
  + [inbound_action_kind] is interrupt_resolution_request
  + [authority_sensitive_action] is work_request
  + [authority_sensitive_action] is claim_request
  + [authority_sensitive_action] is human_override_request
  + [authority_sensitive_action] is interrupt_resolution_request
  + [required_route] is accepted operator contract, SOP-first interrupt, coordination review, or completion review gate
  + [forbidden_route] is direct write to canonical specification, accepted pack, completion review, or source authority from adapter input

  = must: preserve the carrier surface, actor, timestamp, source_ref_set, and intended mutation as traceable context
  = must: classify unsupported or ambiguous inbound actions as SOP-first interrupt rather than silent mutation

& [ForbiddenSurfaceMutationList: FSC4] is the forbidden mutation set for FSC4-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC1, FSC2, or FSC3 output files to make projections easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating UI state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating adapter transport state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating Langflow diagrams as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing UI components
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing adapters or transports
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing Langflow or runtime packages
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching real work
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control
  + [forbidden_mutation] is omitting authority_notice from a decision-making projection

  = must: fail FSC4-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: FSC4] is the stale trigger set for FSC4 downstream work
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC3 runtime graph proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC4 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is surface projection invariant changes
  + [stale_trigger] is authority notice contract changes after manager or worker projection work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is manager or worker projection contract changes after narrative, debug, or adapter projection work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is narrative or debug projection contract changes after adapter projection work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is conversation or adapter projection contract changes after fixture planning starts
  + [stale_trigger] is imported runtime trace proof changes
  + [stale_trigger] is missing authority_notice is detected
  + [stale_trigger] is surface projection hides blocked, stale, faulted, interrupted, or pending-review state
  + [stale_trigger] is adapter mutation bypasses accepted operator, interrupt, coordination, or completion review route

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review rather than silent edits

& [FSC4S01AcceptanceChecklist] is the verification checklist for FSC4-S01
  + [required_component] is imported surface contract inventory
  + [required_component] is projection-owned invariant set
  + [required_component] is surface non-authority boundary
  + [required_component] is adapter mutation boundary
  + [required_component] is forbidden surface mutation list
  + [required_component] is downstream stale trigger list
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is UI implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is transport implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is Langflow export implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime graph implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control

  = must: accept FSC4-S01 only when surface imports are mapped without creating implementation authority
